The button is between D2 and GND (INPUT_PULLUP) and the LED is on D13. When you press the button and hold it down, the LED flashes like mad; the goal is for it to flip once per press. There is one bug in the code. What is it?

```
int onceki = HIGH;
int ledDurum = LOW;

void loop() {
  int simdi = digitalRead(2);
  if (onceki == HIGH && simdi == LOW) {
    ledDurum = 1 - ledDurum;
    digitalWrite(13, ledDurum);
  }
}
```

The button is between D2 and GND (INPUT_PULLUP), and the LED is on D13 and starts off. In this debounced program you press the button, hold it for a while, then let go. When does the LED flip?

```
int onceki = HIGH;
int ledDurum = LOW;

void loop() {
  int simdi = digitalRead(2);
  if (simdi != onceki) {
    delay(20);
    simdi = digitalRead(2);
    if (simdi != onceki) {
      if (simdi == HIGH) {
        ledDurum = 1 - ledDurum;
        digitalWrite(13, ledDurum);
      }
      onceki = simdi;
    }
  }
}
```
